  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>C7.S1 — Order finding by hand</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<div style="background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:5px solid #026573;border-radius:8px;padding:16px 22px;margin-bottom:14px;"><p style="color:#026573;font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;margin:0;">C7.S1 — The arithmetic of the reduction</p></div><p>Take \(N=15\) and \(a=7\).</p><p>(a) Give \(r=\mathrm{ord}_{15}(7)\).</p><p>\(r=\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</p><p>(b) Give \(7^{r/2}\bmod 15\).</p><p>[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]]</p><p>(c) Give the two non-trivial factors \(\gcd(7^{r/2}\pm1,15)\), as an ordered list <code>[smaller, larger]</code>.</p><p>[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) \(7^1=7,\ 7^2=49\equiv4,\ 7^3\equiv28\equiv13,\ 7^4\equiv91\equiv1\pmod{15}\), so \(r=4\).</p><p>(b) \(7^{2}=49\equiv4\pmod{15}\). Crucially \(4\not\equiv-1\equiv14\), so the reduction succeeds.</p><p>(c) \(\gcd(3,15)=3\) and \(\gcd(5,15)=5\), giving \(15=3\cdot5\).</p><p>Had we drawn \(a=14\), we would have \(r=2\) and \(14^{1}\equiv-1\), the failure case — which is why the algorithm retries with a fresh random \(a\). The failure probability is at most \(1/2\) per attempt.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
